# Urwin and Danika Martikov of the Blue Water Inn (docs/voice/urwin_martikov.md, docs/voice/danika_martikov.md).
# urwin: behind the bar (shop). danika: in the kitchen. council: Urwin speaking for the town, if the town won.

~ urwin
if flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Urwin: We'll still give you a bed. Danika says it's what you do. We won't sell you anything. I say that's what you do.
-> END
endif
if not flag.keepers_of_the_feather_met and not flag.raven_harmed and (flag.vallaki_backed == "neither" or (flag.festival_over and flag.bones_returned) or (flag.raven_fed and flag.bones_returned))
-> keepers
endif
if not flag.martikovs_met
set martikovs_met
Narrator: The man behind the bar has black hair, black eyes and the stillness of somebody who has been listening to the room since before you came into it.
if flag.raven_harmed
Narrator: He looks at you for a long moment before he speaks, the way you'd look at someone you have already heard about, and not kindly.
Urwin: Bed's upstairs. Meal's on the stove. Leave the birds on the roof alone.
else
Urwin: Bed's upstairs, meal's on the stove. Questions are free. I might not answer them.
endif
else
Urwin: Back. Good.
endif
-> urwin_menu

~ urwin_menu
* Let's see what you're selling. -> trade
* What's the talk in town? -> rumors
* [if guest:ireena and not flag.bones_returned] Can Ireena stay here for now? -> ireena_room
* [if flag.vallaki_pledge != "town" and not flag.festival_begun] Whose side are you on, the Baron's or Lady Wachter's? -> sides
* [Insight DC 15] There's something he's not saying. -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* Goodbye. -> END

~ trade
Urwin: Bread, candles, oil, rope. One potion; a traveller paid his bill with it and then didn't need it. Prices are fair. Fairer than Bildrath's, anyway.
shop
-> urwin_menu

~ rumors
if not flag.bones_returned
Urwin: Lucian's stripped his altar. Something's gone from the church that shouldn't have. Milivoj the gravedigger is spending more on bread than he earns.
endif
if not flag.wachter_cult_broken and not flag.festival_over
Urwin: Lady Wachter's cellar lamps burn till dawn. Her book club. Nobody's ever seen a book go in.
endif
if not flag.arabelle_rescued and not flag.arabelle_lost
Urwin: The Vistani headman outside the walls has lost his girl. His brother doesn't seem to mind much. That's worth thinking about.
endif
Urwin: And the coffin maker's had a delivery he won't talk about. Big crates. In the night.
-> urwin_menu

~ ireena_room
leave ireena
set ireena_sanctuary = "inn"
quest sanctuary_for_ireena at_inn
Urwin: The room over ours. Nothing comes in through our windows that we don't let in.
Ireena: That's a strange thing for an innkeeper to promise.
Urwin: It's a strange inn.
if guest:ismark
* Ismark, stay with your sister. -> ismark_stays
* Ismark, we need you with us. -> ismark_goes
endif
-> urwin_menu

~ ismark_stays
leave ismark
set ismark_guards_ireena
Ismark: Fine. I'll sit in the taproom and drink Urwin's wine and glare at the door. It's a sacrifice, but I'm prepared to make it.
-> urwin_menu

~ ismark_goes
Ismark: Right. Urwin, if anything so much as looks at her...
Urwin: It won't get the chance.
-> urwin_menu

~ sides
Urwin: Mine. The town's. If you mean the Baron or the widow: neither. Vargas puts people in the stocks for frowning. Fiona would put them in the ground for him, and smile while she did it.
* Then we'll stand with the town too. -> pledge_town
* Fair enough. -> urwin_menu

~ pledge_town
if flag.vallaki_pledge == "baron"
set baron_betrayed
elif flag.vallaki_pledge == "wachter"
set wachter_betrayed
endif
set vallaki_pledge = "town"
quest festival_of_the_blazing_sun town_side
attitude urwin_martikov friendly
Urwin: Then talk to Lucian. He's better with words. When it comes to the festival, there'll be more of us in the crowd than you'll think. Keep your eyes on the rooftops.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +2 thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +2 liriel_dawnsong +2 kip_smudgewick +1 ratatoille +1: You stood with the people of Vallaki, against both of them
-> urwin_menu

~ insight_ok
Narrator: He watches the windows more than the door. Each time a bird lands on the sill, he glances at it the way a man glances at a friend, and once you'd swear it nodded back.
-> urwin_menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: He polishes a cup that doesn't need polishing and gives you nothing. He's done this before, to better questioners than you.
-> urwin_menu

~ keepers
set keepers_of_the_feather_met
set wizard_of_wines_hook
cutscene keepers_ravens
Narrator: Urwin closes the shutters, one after another, and when he turns round there are ravens on every beam of the taproom: a dozen, two dozen, silent, all watching you.
if flag.raven_fed
Urwin: A friend of ours walked beside you on the road and you fed him. Then you stood by this town. That makes you friends of ours.
else
Urwin: You stood between this town and the people who'd sell it. That makes you friends of ours.
endif
Urwin: We're the Keepers of the Feather. We watch. We carry word. Some nights we fly.
Urwin: My father keeps a vineyard south of here: the Wizard of Wines. The wine's stopped coming, and so has word from him. When you're on that road, go to him. Tell him Urwin sent you. The ravens will know you.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Did one of them just wink at me? I winked back. Was that right?
else
interject tag:curious: Did one of them just wink at me?
endif
Urwin: Probably. Don't encourage him.
-> END

~ council
Urwin: Council business. Grain, lamp oil, who mends the palisade. Not a festival in sight. I've never been so happy to be bored.
if flag.wachter_fate == "free"
Urwin: Fiona's still in her house, smiling at us through the window. One day she'll make a mistake, and we'll be watching when she does.
endif
-> END

~ danika
if flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Danika [angry]: You did this. I know you did; the whole town watched you do it. You'll get a bed, because I won't turn anyone into the night. Don't expect breakfast.
-> END
endif
if not flag.danika_met
set danika_met
Narrator: A woman with flour to the elbows looks up from a cauldron, takes in your boots and your weapons, and decides you can stay.
Danika: Guests. Wipe your feet. Brom! Bray! Get away from that window. Sorry. Two boys and an inn. You'd think one would cancel out the other.
endif
* What's good to eat? -> eat
* [if not flag.wizard_of_wines_hook] The wine at the bar is thin. -> wine
* [if guest:ireena] Will Ireena be safe here? -> ireena_safe
* Goodbye. -> END

~ eat
Danika: Stew. It's always stew. What's in it depends what Urwin found. Don't ask him, and don't ask the stew.
-> danika

~ wine
set wizard_of_wines_hook
Danika: Thin? It's the last cask. The wine comes from Urwin's father's vineyard, the Wizard of Wines, south of the lake road. Every month, a cart. Three months now, no cart, and no word.
if flag.wine_shortage_heard
interject tag:curious: The tavern in the village of Barovia is out too. The barkeep said the deliveries had stopped.
Danika: Then it's not just us. Then something's wrong at the vineyard. I'll tell Urwin. He'll want to know where you heard it.
endif
approve ratatoille +1: You told the Blue Water's barmaid her wine was thin
-> danika

~ ireena_safe
Danika: Safe as anyone in this valley. Safer than most. Our windows have very good locks, and better neighbours.
-> danika
